# Zenodo: after the first GitHub release, add the concept DOI here as  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.NNNNNNN
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Systems analysis: open tools with an evidence ledger"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, and the method of the tool you used (see src/<tool>/CITATION.cff)."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Inderwildi
    given-names: Oliver
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliverinderwildi/systems-analysis"
url: "https://oliverinderwildi.github.io/code/"
abstract: >-
  A collection of open tools for systems analysis - fault tree analysis, event tree analysis, and analysis of competing hypotheses - each a faithful implementation of a published method with credit to its authors, plus a shared kernel that records where every input came from.
keywords:
  - systems analysis
  - fault tree analysis
  - event tree analysis
  - analysis of competing hypotheses
  - provenance
  - evidence ledger
